# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# The watchdog PD services the hardware watchdog's
# stand-in for ten rounds, each ended by the stand-in's 200 ms tick, while
# the supervisor and three probes answer their heartbeats; then looper loops
# and starves lower, and at round 11 the watchdog names both, highest
# priority first, and stops servicing; three ticks later the stand-in says
# the hardware would now reset the board.
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children watchdog (0), timer (1), stand_in (2), upper (3), looper (4) and lower (5)
NOWAYOS: watchdog: watching 4 PDs, highest priority first: watchdog_supervisor, upper, looper, lower
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: a tick to the watchdog every 200 ms; unserviced for 3 ticks, the hardware would reset the board
NOWAYOS: heartbeat-probe: upper answering its heartbeat
NOWAYOS: heartbeat-probe: looper answering its heartbeat
NOWAYOS: heartbeat-probe: lower answering its heartbeat
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 1: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 2: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 3: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 4: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 5: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 6: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 7: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 8: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 9: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 10: every PD answered; hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: heartbeat-probe: looper: looping from now on, after 10 answers, starving every PD below it
NOWAYOS: watchdog: round 11: no answer from looper, lower (highest priority first); the hardware watchdog is no longer serviced and will reset the board
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: serviced 10 times, then not for 3 ticks (600 ms): the hardware would now reset the board

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault the monitor or the supervisor saw, a kernel error message, a PD
# giving up, the watchdog unable to watch, servicing after a miss, or the
# reset coming before looper loops.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!stopped:
!NOT stopped
!gave up
!cannot watch
!round 12
!panicked
